{
  "schema": "chain-hit-reactions/1",
  "about": "ALIVE hit-reaction rows for the chain bodies. Data only: the game's bone-maths layer (ARMAGEDOM hit-reaction.js) reads a row by body + zone + dir, maps part ids to bones through boneMap, and lays an additive lean/twist on the playing clip; physics applies rd.stagger({ part, impulse }) from the same row. Start values from a geometry rule (docs/API.md, chain hit reactions); retune on our clips.",
  "frame": {"forward":"+z","up":"+y","left":"+x","note":"Body frame = the ragdoll's rest frame (head toward +z). dir names the side the blow comes FROM. Part ids named L/R follow the rig and may be mirrored: the legs rows are by geometry (x sign), never by the letter."},
  "zones": ["head","front_body","rear_body","legs","tail"],
  "dirs": ["front","back","left","right"],
  "impulse_dirs": {"front":[0,0,-1],"back":[0,0,1],"left":[-1,0,0],"right":[1,0,0]},
  "weights_note": "weights[partId] = [bend, twist]. bend 0..1: the share of the class lean the part takes, pitched along impulse_dir (away from the blow). twist -1..1: the share of the class twist, yaw about +y, positive = nose toward +x (the body's left), negative toward -x. Parts not listed take 0.",
  "impulse_note": "Physics impulse = impulse_dir x impulse_scale x class power x mass_kg of the struck part (a velocity change of impulse_scale x power m/s). hold_s is how long the bone-maths layer holds the pose; the physics motor dip runs on data/states.json stagger.",
  "no_joints": ["drone"],
